From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 23:39:27 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] smp: log the T8132 CPU_START status words around each
 secondary start

cpu_start_bit() indexes the T8132 global start/status mask by cpu-id, as on
T8142. That is inferred, not measured. Print CPU_START +0x0 and +0x4 before
and after each T8132 start, together with the bit m1n1 wrote, so a single
boot shows which bit each cpu-id owns. If a secondary fails to start, the
same line shows how far the status got. The values are read-only, from
registers m1n1 already writes at this point. Other SoCs are unchanged.

The line reaches the m1n1 console and the m1n1_stage2.log phram buffer
(dt_setup_mtd_phram), as raw hex words, so the boot log alone is enough to
read it. test_smp_legacy_rvbar.py defines T8132 for the new branch.

Hardware tested on: NOT YET
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 src/smp.c                             | 14 ++++++++++++++
 tests/python/test_smp_legacy_rvbar.py |  1 +
 2 files changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/smp.c b/src/smp.c
index ebad55b2..8b539ba5 100644
--- a/src/smp.c
+++ b/src/smp.c
@@ -363,6 +363,16 @@ static int smp_start_cpu(int index, const struct cpu_info *cpu)
     }
 
     u64 start_base = cpu_start_base + cpu->die * PMGR_DIE_OFFSET;
+    /*
+     * T8132's CPU_START mask layout is inferred from T8142 (cpu_start_bit()).
+     * Log the global status words around each start so one boot shows which
+     * bit each cpu-id owns. Read-only; m1n1 already writes these registers.
+     */
+    u32 status0 = 0, status4 = 0;
+    if (chip_id == T8132) {
+        status0 = read32(start_base + 0x0);
+        status4 = read32(start_base + 0x4);
+    }
 
     // Some kind of system level startup/status bit
     // Without this, IRQs don't work
@@ -383,6 +393,10 @@ static int smp_start_cpu(int index, const struct cpu_info *cpu)
     } else {
         printf("  Started.\n");
     }
+    if (chip_id == T8132)
+        printf("SMP: CPU %d bit 0x%x CPU_START +0 0x%x->0x%x +4 0x%x->0x%x\n", index,
+               cpu_start_bit(index, cpu), status0, read32(start_base + 0x0), status4,
+               read32(start_base + 0x4));
 
     _reset_stack = dummy_stack + DUMMY_STACK_SIZE;
     _reset_stack_el1 = dummy_stack_el1 + DUMMY_STACK_SIZE;
diff --git a/tests/python/test_smp_legacy_rvbar.py b/tests/python/test_smp_legacy_rvbar.py
index 9ff083e3..bdacdea8 100644
--- a/tests/python/test_smp_legacy_rvbar.py
+++ b/tests/python/test_smp_legacy_rvbar.py
@@ -32,6 +32,7 @@ _Static_assert(sizeof(u64) == 8, "production u64 ABI");
 #define T8103 0x8103
 #define T8140 0x8140
 #define T8142 0x8142
+#define T8132 0x8132
 #define T8152 0x8152
 #define MAIR_IDX_NORMAL 0
 #define PERM_RW 0
